eption e) {","+                warning.warn(\"A RateLimitOutcomeListener failed; the request continues\", e);","+            }","+        }","+    }"," }"],"additions":40,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/http-rate-limit/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/http/ratelimit/runtime/internal/telemetry/DevModeRejectionLog.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@","+package io.quarkus.http.ratelimit.runtime.internal.telemetry;","+","+import org.jboss.logging.Logger;","+","+import io.quarkus.http.ratelimit.runtime.internal.rules.RuleEvaluator;","+","+/**","+ * Logs every rejection with its key, so that a developer sees why a request got 429. The key is client input, so it","+ * is {@linkplain LogText#escape escaped}. Registered in dev mode only:","+ * elsewhere rejections are reported through the {@code RateLimitRejectionInfo} event. It therefore has no","+ * bean-defining annotation: the deployment module registers it as a singleton.","+ */","+public class DevModeRejectionLog implements RateLimitOutcomeListener {","+","+    private static final Logger LOG = Logger.getLogger(DevModeRejectionLog.class);","+","+    @Override","+    public void rejected(RuleEvaluator evaluator, String key, long retryAfterSeconds) {","+        LOG.infof(\"Rate limit rule '%s' rejected key '%s' (Retry-After: %ds)\", evaluator.rule(), LogText.escape(key),","+                retryAfterSeconds);","+    }","+}"],"additions":22,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/http-rate-limit/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/http/ratelimit/runtime/internal/telemetry/LogText.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@","+package io.quarkus.http.ratelimit.runtime.internal.telemetry;","+","+/**","+ * Makes request data safe to log: keys and paths are decoded client input, so a CR LF in them would otherwise start a","+ * forged log line, and an escape sequence would drive the terminal that shows the log.","+ */","+public final class LogText {","+","+    private LogText() {","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * @return the text with backslashes, control characters and Unicode line separators escaped as in a Java string","+     *         literal: a doubled backslash, {@code \\r}, {@code \\n}, {@code \\t}, else a backslash, {@code u} and four hex","+     *         digits; the text itself when it contains none","+     */","+    public static String escape(String text) {","+        int i = 0;","+        while (i < text.length() && !needsEscape(text.charAt(i))) {","+            i++;","+        }","+        if (i == text.length()) {","+            return text;","+        }","+        StringBuilder escaped = new StringBuilder(text.length() + 16).append(text, 0, i);","+        for (; i < text.length(); i++) {","+            char c = text.charAt(i);","+            switch (c) {","+                case '\\\\' -> escaped.append(\"\\\\\\\\\");","+                case '\\r' -> escaped.append(\"\\\\r\");","+                case '\\n' -> escaped.append(\"\\\\n\");","+                case '\\t' -> escaped.append(\"\\\\t\");","+                default -> {","+                    if (needsEscape(c)) {","+                        escaped.append(String.format(\"\\\\u%04x\", (int) c));","+                    } else {","+                        escaped.append(c);","+                    }","+                }","+            }","+        }","+        return escaped.toString();","+    }","+","+    private static boolean needsEscape(char c) {","+        // U+2028 LINE SEPARATOR and U+2029 PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR: some log viewers and terminals show them as a line break","+        return c == '\\\\' || Character.isISOControl(c) || c == '\\u2028' || c == '\\u2029';","+    }","+}"],"additions":49,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/http-rate-limit/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/http/ratelimit/runtime/internal/telemetry/RateLimitOutcomeListener.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@","+package io.quarkus.http.ratelimit.runtime.internal.telemetry;","+","+import io.quarkus.http.ratelimit.runtime.internal.rules.RuleEvaluator;","+","+/**","+ * Internal hook told about the admissions and rejections of a rule, such as the dev-mode rejection log. Implementations","+ * are CDI beans, run on the event loop and must not block.","+ */","+public interface RateLimitOutcomeListener {","+","+    /**","+     * The rule admitted the request.","+     *","+     * @param remaining the whole permits the store reports as left","+     */","+    default void allowed(RuleEvaluator evaluator, long remaining) {","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * The rule rejected the request with 429.","+     *","+     * @param key the key that was rejected","+     * @param retryAfterSeconds the value of the {@code Retry-After} header","+     */","+    default void rejected(RuleEvaluator evaluator, String key, long retryAfterSeconds) {","+    }","+}"],"additions":27,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/http-rate-limit/runtime/src/test/java/io/quarkus/http/ratelimit/runtime/internal/telemetry/LogTextTest.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@","+package io.quarkus.http.ratelimit.runtime.internal.telemetry;","+","+import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;","+","+import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;","+","+class LogTextTest {","+","+    @Test","+    void plainTextIsUnchanged() {","+        String text = \"path:/api/users/é\";","+        assertThat(LogText.escape(text)).isSameAs(text);","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    void controlCharactersAndSeparatorsAreEscaped() {","+        assertThat(LogText.escape(\"a\\r\\nINFO forged\\t\\u001b[31m\\u0000\\u007f \\\\\"))","+                .isEqualTo(\"a\\\\r\\\\nINFO forged\\\\t\\\\u001b[31m\\\\u0000\\\\u007f\\\\u2028\\\\\\\\\");","+    }","+}",""],"additions":20,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":274,"deletions":4,"truncated":false,"file_count":8},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-19T17:59:29.889788+00:00"}